# Instance-owned files: framework tag-merges never overwrite these.
# Git uses the "ours" merge strategy for any merge (including `git merge <tag>`),
# keeping this instance's version and discarding the incoming framework change.
#
# This is instance #1 (lagunabeach.md), re-based onto the sekai-kb framework in
# task 5.4. The list below extends the framework baseline
# (place.config.ts, knowledge/**, public/media/**, CNAME, CLAUDE.md, README.md)
# with the two instance-owned paths minted in the 5.4 packet:
#   docs/baselines/**  and  scripts/ci/genericity-denylist.local.txt
# See docs/runbook/UPGRADE.md §Instance-owned files. Add your own below.

place.config.ts merge=ours
knowledge/** merge=ours
public/media/** merge=ours
CNAME merge=ours
CLAUDE.md merge=ours
README.md merge=ours
docs/baselines/** merge=ours
scripts/ci/genericity-denylist.local.txt merge=ours
